1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you!

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, it's so elusive!

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me!

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,677
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you!

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see!

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,897
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:12,520
Believe in what I do!

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,617
We don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,677
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,460
We live in one another.

26
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:56,617
Everyone!

27
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:58,560
We found Dalton over here!

28
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:00,800
What? Yeah!

29
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:02,310
Fantastic!

30
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:03,610
We're coming!

31
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:04,800
Dalton!

32
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:07,220
Who's Dalton?

33
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:16,780
This is horrible I can't feel a heartbeat.

34
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:25,577
I've prepared this extra nutritious and
fortifying meal just for you so we can

35
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:31,377
get a healthy smile back on that beautiful
face of yours thank you Sanji of course

36
00:02:31,460 --> 00:02:34,917
Although you're as heartbreakingly
gorgeous as ever in spite of your painful

37
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,300
ordeal Hey you I don't recall you asking
for permission to use my kitchen Madam,

38
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:41,957
I made a dish for you as well.

39
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:44,334
It's supposed to make you look years...

40
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:45,840
I'm not a madam.

41
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:49,297
I'm a swinging single
still in the prime of you.

42
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:50,317
Don't forget it.

43
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:53,380
Not a day over 139, right? Dr.

44
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:55,557
Lee, save me from this loaded tape!

45
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:57,140
Wait, hold on, come back!

46
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:05,780
What are you doing? Luffy?

47
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:08,749
This guy's gonna join
us and be our friend!

48
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,360
Really? Great!

49
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,417
I didn't say I was going to do that!

50
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:13,330
Sure you did!

51
00:03:13,413 --> 00:03:14,243
No, I didn't!

52
00:03:14,326 --> 00:03:16,620
Be quiet, both of you!

53
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,190
Friend, huh?

54
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:26,165
If he only knew what friend means to
someone who's been through what Chopper has.

55
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:28,150
Poor guy.

56
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:31,740
When Chopper was out there on his own,

57
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:35,717
there was only one human that
he ever really opened up to.

58
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:38,560
That man's name was Dr. Hiriluk.

59
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:43,260
He was a crazy quack, but he named
Chopper and called him his son.

60
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,880
Hey, you! Stop!

61
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,430
Where'd he go?

62
00:03:53,513 --> 00:03:55,057
He beats me, and he disappeared.

63
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:56,040
Crazy quack!

64
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,660
We've got to get him!

65
00:03:57,900 --> 00:04:01,040
Those are Lord Waple's
orders. Now move out! Right!

66
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:18,197
You can't go on like this.

67
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:19,757
We have to call a doctor.

68
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:21,197
We can't.

69
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:23,280
There are no doctors left to call.

70
00:04:23,860 --> 00:04:26,377
Except for the 20 mds who belong to Wapol.

71
00:04:26,460 --> 00:04:30,277
If we have to beg Wapol on our knees
for help then that's what we have to do.

72
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,237
I'll go get them.

73
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:33,144
You don't need waple's charity.

74
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:41,240
I'll examine him. Here, look!

75
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:42,940
No, I'm fine.

76
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,077
It's just a cold.

77
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:47,537
Besides, the last bunch of patients you
treated ended up getting a whole lot worse.

78
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,777
Now, there's no need to
be shy with your doctor.

79
00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:53,157
I just developed a wonderful
new old-purpose drug yesterday.

80
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,360
You're a lucky man.

81
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:55,290
Now, shut up.

82
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:01,877
Oh, that's not the kind
of gun you think it is.

83
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:04,397
It's a tranquilizer gun for
patients with severe pain.

84
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,245
I'm going to get the soldiers.

85
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:10,857
Please go if you want money I'll be glad

86
00:05:10,940 --> 00:05:14,677
to pay I don't take
money from sick people.

87
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:20,040
I just want to help you don't do
it please I'm too young to die.

88
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:32,017
Huh okay I gotta admit
I wasn't expecting that

89
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:34,257
I must have made a mistake
with the ingredients.

90
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:35,170
somehow.

91
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:37,577
Guess I shouldn't have used frog extract.

92
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:39,680
Uh, sorry there. My mistake.

93
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:41,050
Pyrrha, look!

94
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:41,963
Are you in there?

95
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,550
Hold it!

96
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:57,440
Are you happy now? Quack!

97
00:05:58,460 --> 00:05:59,290
The Dr.

98
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,317
Hunt has reached its final stage.

99
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:04,635
I hear you and I are the only
ones left in the country.

100
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:08,337
Wapol has his hunters desperately
looking for us everywhere.

101
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:12,117
And even if they weren't, you'd
already be a pariah in this country.

102
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:14,612
Since you're the worst quack of them all.

103
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:21,497
I'm not going to get caught
by some fool doctor hunt.

104
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:25,404
And one day I'll end up saving
this country with medical science.

105
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:26,920
Yeah, right.

106
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:29,297
I think you mean destroy this country.

107
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:31,357
Look, there are people on the bridge.

108
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:32,677
See you around, quack.

109
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:35,540
Not if I see you first,
you thieving sawbones.

110
00:06:44,260 --> 00:06:46,789
Those tin soldiers
aren't gonna capture me.

111
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:49,802
I'm gonna go on helping
the sick and the injured.

112
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:57,637
Looks like you've been shot.

113
00:06:57,720 --> 00:07:00,955
We need to stop the bleeding
right away or you're dead.

114
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:02,110
Don't worry.

115
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,380
I'll save you.

116
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,800
It's a Yeti! Shoot it!

117
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:10,037
Actually, you're pretty lucky,

118
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:14,944
because I just created an ointment three
days ago that even works on broken bones.

119
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:20,577
We can't let that Blue
Moose Yeti get away, man!

120
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:21,490
Kill him before he kills us!

121
00:07:21,573 --> 00:07:22,403
Shoot him down!

122
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,437
Just what are you, anyway?

123
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:30,560
You don't look like a human being.

124
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:34,506
You must be that Yeti everyone
is talking about in the village.

125
00:07:47,140 --> 00:07:48,360
Yeah! We got him!

126
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:50,440
It wasn't enough. Finish him!

127
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,520
How dare you?

128
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:08,120
Who do you think you're
dealing with, creature?

129
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:09,900
Hey, wait!

130
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:15,500
I promise I'm not gonna shoot you, see?

131
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:21,520
My name is Hiriluk, Dr. Hiriluk!

132
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:24,520
And I wanna help you!

133
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:30,494
It's not a good thing.

134
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:31,877
It's a pretty good thing.

135
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,257
You'll have to go to the next one.

136
00:08:33,340 --> 00:08:34,170
This is just a good thing.

137
00:08:34,253 --> 00:08:35,083
Well, I wonder if I am doing something.

138
00:08:35,166 --> 00:08:58,460
I'm going to go.

139
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:21,360
That was the first encounter
between Chopper and Dr. Hiriluk.

140
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:25,000
So, what happened next?

141
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:27,760
Between Chopper and Dr. Hiriluk?

142
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:31,740
Wait, you can talk?

143
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:38,280
Why have you kept silent?

144
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:41,660
I thought you'd hate me if I talked.

145
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,235
When I talked to humans the
other day, they shot at me.

146
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:49,840
You see, people think
I'm a freak for that.

147
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:52,200
So you can talk, so what?

148
00:09:53,740 --> 00:09:55,460
Even children learn to talk.

149
00:09:55,680 --> 00:09:58,092
I don't see what's damn special about it.

150
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:00,710
Ah!

151
00:10:00,793 --> 00:10:01,623
Run, Chopper!

152
00:10:08,840 --> 00:10:11,037
Aw, I thought for sure that would work.

153
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:12,708
Hey, Chopper, are you okay?

154
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:17,090
Eh?

155
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:20,691
Well, at least your head was
bandaged to begin with, right?

156
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:28,040
Hey, did you call me Chopper?

157
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:30,060
That's your new name, Tony.

158
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:31,260
Tony Chopper.

159
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:33,437
I picked it because I
thought you'd look like you

160
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:36,477
could chop down a tree with
those antlers of yours.

161
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:37,640
Cool name, huh?

162
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:40,951
Anyway, that's what I'm going to call you.

163
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:43,650
Sir.

164
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:49,020
Now listen up, Chopper.

165
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:51,597
Always pay close attention
to your patient's

166
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:53,597
symptoms and give them proper treatment.

167
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:55,974
That's the way to save a person's life.

168
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:58,980
Let's go.

169
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:01,700
There are sick people who need my help.

170
00:11:02,020 --> 00:11:03,961
Get out of here, you crazy clown!

171
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:07,520
I thought lizard eyeballs would work!

172
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:11,000
Don't ever come back! Girls!

173
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:14,080
It's Waffle's guards! Run!

174
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:16,957
Chopper, it's time to use the decoy plant!

175
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:17,922
The wood plant?

176
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:19,140
Good luck, pal!

177
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:27,560
You almost got me killed,
you maniac! So what?

178
00:11:27,660 --> 00:11:30,857
You already cheated death once,
you clumsy Pluto's caribou?

179
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,697
That's reindeer and don't call me Pluto!

180
00:11:32,780 --> 00:11:33,610
Hey!

181
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:50,580
Doctor, that's the first time
I've ever fought with anyone.

182
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:55,037
I can believe that.

183
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:57,355
You have to have an opponent to fight.

184
00:11:57,620 --> 00:12:00,320
So is it your first time for this as well?

185
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:07,240
That's for you. A gift.

186
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:09,440
As a memento of our making up.

187
00:12:10,660 --> 00:12:11,490
Gift?

188
00:12:11,573 --> 00:12:12,403
Making up?

189
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:24,840
You know, Chopper, it sometimes
feels that things are pretty rough.

190
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:28,740
But try not to hold a grudge
against us humans, okay?

191
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:30,940
This country is sick right now.

192
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:35,337
The people and the king both suffer
from a terrible sickness of the heart.

193
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:38,757
The conventional wisdom has it that
there is no way to cure a sick country.

194
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:39,840
But that's wrong.

195
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:44,971
Once my invention has been perfected,
this country will be as good as saved.

196
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:50,000
You see, there used to be a master thief
who lived in a country in the far west.

197
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:52,041
He had a serious heart condition.

198
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:56,557
He went to the greatest doctors he
could find to receive treatment.

199
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:58,522
But no one was able to cure him.

200
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:00,700
They told him he was going to die.

201
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:04,352
Frustrated and depressed, he
passed by a certain mountain.

202
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:07,384
There he saw something
he had never seen before.

203
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:17,150
Blossoms!

204
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:20,142
He saw cherry blossoms
all over the mountainside.

205
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:23,617
And then he went to see another doctor and

206
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:26,500
got the shock of his
life because he was told,

207
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:28,237
you're perfectly healthy.

208
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:29,260
Huh?

209
00:13:29,780 --> 00:13:32,700
He was cured. It was a
miracle. Don't you see?

210
00:13:32,940 --> 00:13:35,777
But it also makes perfect
sense medically speaking.

211
00:13:35,860 --> 00:13:37,297
By changing his emotional state,

212
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:40,498
he was able to change his
physical state somehow too.

213
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:45,034
And if that's true, there's no disease
in this world that can't be cured.

214
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:46,840
Let them laugh at me.

215
00:13:47,020 --> 00:13:49,780
My medical skills will
save this country yet.

216
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:54,280
And that's why I raised
this skull and cross bones.

217
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:57,324
As a challenge to all the
diseases of the world.

218
00:13:58,400 --> 00:14:02,660
This symbolizes my belief
that nothing is impossible.

219
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,420
I will save this country
with my doctor's skills.

220
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:12,040
By raising this flag, I vow to
fight just like the pirates do.

221
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,000
Hey, reindeer!

222
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:17,540
Join us and be our friend!

223
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:20,390
Booty!

224
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:28,700
I don't be a pirate!

225
00:14:30,560 --> 00:14:33,440
Doctor, what are pirates? Pirates?

226
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:37,537
They're dashing
swashbucklers of the sea with

227
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:40,077
great strength and the eyesight of eagles.

228
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:42,500
Their voices echo like rolling thunder.

229
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:46,780
Hey, you're really a pirate? Huh?

230
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:49,200
Well, yeah, of course I am.

231
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:51,417
It's like I've been saying all along.

232
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:54,437
We do all kinds of fun stuff,
like fishing and singing.

233
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:55,350
Huh?

234
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:57,190
Huh?

235
00:14:57,273 --> 00:14:58,103
Pirates sing?

236
00:14:58,186 --> 00:14:59,016
Sure we do.

237
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:00,657
And sometimes we dance, too.

238
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:02,437
You call that being a pirate?

239
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:03,480
Of course.

240
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:06,240
And we go on adventures. You really do?

241
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:08,559
Pirates really do go on adventures?

242
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:10,280
Yeah, you bet we do.

243
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:12,657
Pirates risk their lives
to go on adventures.

244
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:14,960
And you meet the most amazing people.

245
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,789
It's great to be a pirate.

246
00:15:17,020 --> 00:15:19,420
The most amazing people sail the seas.

247
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,837
Chopper, someday you've got to go to sea.

248
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:24,800
If you do,

249
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,157
you'll realize just how
small your problems really

250
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:29,897
are in comparison to the
vastness of the oceans.

251
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:33,686
The island you were born on is
like this compared to the world.

252
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,150
Really?

253
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:37,620
No, it's smaller, like this.

254
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:39,110
Really?

255
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:47,160
Your destiny lies beyond that shining sea.

256
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:50,980
The good times passed in
the twinkling of an eye.

257
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:54,020
and then

258
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:04,760
it finally came time to say farewell.

