521
00:33:43,913 --> 00:33:48,360
Hey, when do you think a person dies?

522
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:55,180
When a bullet from a pistol
pierces his heart? No.

523
00:33:56,580 --> 00:33:59,920
When he's attacked by an
incurable disease? No.

524
00:34:00,740 --> 00:34:04,900
When he eats a soup of deadly
poisonous mushrooms? No!

525
00:34:06,340 --> 00:34:10,180
A man dies when people forget him.

526
00:34:11,640 --> 00:34:15,287
Even if I should disappear right
now, my dream will come true.

527
00:34:15,380 --> 00:34:19,851
And when it does, the citizen's sickness
of the heart will be cured as well.

528
00:34:20,920 --> 00:34:22,017
You're crying?

529
00:34:22,100 --> 00:34:23,260
Why, Dalton?

530
00:34:25,020 --> 00:34:27,840
Is that true for a country?

531
00:34:29,160 --> 00:34:31,660
Yeah, if the will to do it is passed on.

532
00:34:32,180 --> 00:34:33,220
Come on, Dalton!

533
00:34:33,460 --> 00:34:34,600
Why are you crying?

534
00:34:38,640 --> 00:34:41,200
Very shortly, a monster will be coming.

535
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:43,440
He's my son.

536
00:34:44,380 --> 00:34:45,820
Please, don't hurt him.

537
00:34:48,060 --> 00:34:49,500
Don't worry, Chopper.

538
00:34:50,160 --> 00:34:52,760
Your mushroom won't kill me.

539
00:34:56,160 --> 00:34:59,340
I've had a marvelous life!

540
00:35:00,320 --> 00:35:02,420
Goodbye, Quack.

541
00:35:03,720 --> 00:35:05,880
Thank you, Chopper!

542
00:35:28,660 --> 00:35:30,760
He blew himself off!

543
00:35:30,960 --> 00:35:32,120
What an idiot!

544
00:35:40,380 --> 00:35:42,680
Oh, crap! It's nothing!

545
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:43,840
It's a monster!

546
00:35:44,420 --> 00:35:45,250
Shoot him!

547
00:35:45,333 --> 00:35:46,500
Shoot him! Stop!

548
00:35:52,560 --> 00:35:53,390
Leave!

549
00:35:53,473 --> 00:35:54,580
Leave here at once!

550
00:35:54,880 --> 00:35:58,580
If you can't even defeat me,
you can't possibly defeat them!

551
00:36:02,360 --> 00:36:06,419
I apologize for those who had the
nerve to laugh at Hyruleuk's death.

552
00:36:08,580 --> 00:36:11,404
Without enough strength,
you'd only die in vain.

553
00:36:13,520 --> 00:36:15,140
Don't waste your life.

554
00:36:16,100 --> 00:36:18,340
Don't sacrifice it for this country.

555
00:36:20,480 --> 00:36:21,310
Please.

556
00:36:21,780 --> 00:36:22,610
Huh?

557
00:36:25,340 --> 00:36:26,900
You let him get away!

558
00:36:27,320 --> 00:36:28,555
Just shut your mouth!

559
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:31,017
The only man who cared
enough to try to cure

560
00:36:31,100 --> 00:36:33,917
this sick country has just
died while you laughed!

561
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:36,882
Even while everyone else
just gave up in despair,

562
00:36:37,220 --> 00:36:40,632
this kind doctor attempted to
save us all and died for it!

563
00:36:41,580 --> 00:36:43,840
So what if someone like that dies?

564
00:36:44,480 --> 00:36:46,877
I've seen the path this
country should take.

565
00:36:46,960 --> 00:36:48,177
It should just die out!

566
00:36:48,260 --> 00:36:50,057
As long as we stay here,

567
00:36:50,140 --> 00:36:53,728
it can't be rebuilt, because
even if medical care progresses,

568
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:55,781
even if medical research goes on,

569
00:36:56,040 --> 00:36:59,820
there is no medicine that can cure fools!

570
00:37:01,240 --> 00:37:07,060
I let you have your say, and all
you've done is make me angry!

571
00:37:10,220 --> 00:37:11,050
Please!

572
00:37:11,260 --> 00:37:13,400
Please teach me how to be a doctor!

573
00:37:14,260 --> 00:37:16,577
You've got to teach me
how to become a doctor.

574
00:37:16,660 --> 00:37:17,490
You've got to.

575
00:37:17,573 --> 00:37:19,417
I'll become the all-purpose medicine.

576
00:37:19,500 --> 00:37:21,777
I'll become a doctor
who can cure anything.

577
00:37:21,860 --> 00:37:22,690
You'll see.

578
00:37:22,800 --> 00:37:24,271
I'll even cure a country.

579
00:37:24,420 --> 00:37:28,097
I'll do anything you ask of me,
but I've got to become a doctor.

580
00:37:28,180 --> 00:37:32,900
Because I know there's no disease, no
illness in this world that can't be cured.

581
00:37:38,340 --> 00:37:39,460
Call me Dr.

582
00:37:39,640 --> 00:37:41,080
Rain from now on.

583
00:37:46,120 --> 00:37:47,500
I won't die.

584
00:37:48,080 --> 00:37:49,120
I'll carry on.

585
00:37:49,700 --> 00:37:50,530
His will.

586
00:37:56,860 --> 00:38:02,920
So for the six years since then, Chopper's
been studying medicine under you. Yeah.

587
00:38:03,420 --> 00:38:05,700
I taught him everything I know.

588
00:38:06,280 --> 00:38:07,860
He's been a good student.

589
00:38:08,720 --> 00:38:10,640
Dr. Ean! Dr. Ean!

590
00:38:11,340 --> 00:38:13,300
Dr. Ean! There's trouble!

591
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:15,300
Waffle is back!

592
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:18,900
Is he?

593
00:38:20,180 --> 00:38:21,010
It's him!

594
00:38:22,520 --> 00:38:24,980
The guy with the annoying mouth!

595
00:38:28,880 --> 00:38:30,880
I have returned, finally!

596
00:38:31,240 --> 00:38:34,260
Now, at long last, we
shall restore Drum Kingdom!

597
00:38:37,800 --> 00:38:39,240
Waffle, sir, look!

598
00:38:39,420 --> 00:38:40,655
On top of the castle!

599
00:38:46,360 --> 00:38:49,400
Why is that strange flag
flying? It's an outrage!

600
00:38:49,700 --> 00:38:51,876
Where's the flag of the Drum Kingdom?

601
00:38:55,240 --> 00:38:57,360
That old thing, I burned it!

602
00:38:57,940 --> 00:39:02,137
Well, Kureha, the last survivor of
our Doctor Hunt, get out of my castle!

603
00:39:02,220 --> 00:39:04,620
This castle is no longer yours, Wapol!

604
00:39:04,880 --> 00:39:07,797
It saw enough corruption and
misery during your reign!

605
00:39:07,880 --> 00:39:08,710
Leave!

606
00:39:08,840 --> 00:39:10,664
Not just here, the country too!

607
00:39:10,920 --> 00:39:13,332
Drum Kingdom has already died out, moron!

608
00:39:14,400 --> 00:39:15,420
What's that?

609
00:39:17,900 --> 00:39:18,730
Wait!

610
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:22,340
This guy is mine!
